 )+/,ee="Claude Code did not run this command: it holds a --transform from the /claude-api managed-agents-secure instructions but is not that `ant` command as written. Run each of those commands alone and exactly as written, with each ID typed inside its single quotes (agent_, env_ or vlt_, then only letters and digits). Add --version only to `ant beta:agents retrieve`, as a whole number with no leading zero. If an ID or version read from the account has another form, do not run the command: ask the developer about it, and mark each report row that needs it CAN'T TELL.",te="Claude Code did not run this command: it holds an ID starting agent_, env_ or vlt_ then staging_, vrtx_ or bdrk_, which `ant` commands may not use. Do not run the command another way: tell the developer which ID was refused and ask where it came from. If this is part of /claude-api managed-agents-secure, mark each report row that needs it CAN'T TELL.",ne="Claude Code did not run this command: it holds an ID starting agent_local_, env_local_ or vlt_local_, and the ID or the command around it is not in the one form Claude Code accepts. Such IDs come from a self-hosted or local Managed Agents server. Each such ID in the command must have the form agent_, env_ or vlt_, then local_01, then 22 letters and digits other than 0, O, I and l, and must be typed in full as its own argument to ant or ant.exe, named in lowercase with no path. Only cd into a folder, or another ant command, may come before ant; do not run ant through or feed it from another program such as timeout, echo or xargs. The command must be Bash made of plain commands joined by &&, || or ;, with at most one | after ant, into a program such as jq. It must not use: & to run a command in the background; VAR=value, export or any other variable setting; a redirect such as > file or 2>&1; if, for, while, case or function; a ( ) or { } group; $ variables; $( ), <( ), >( ) or backtick substitutions; or here-documents or <<< strings. To reach a s